title: Lysozyme nephropathy
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Clinical relevance:'' Rare cause of acute kidney injury in chronic monocytic or [[myelomonocytic leukemia|Chronic myelomonocytic leukemia]].
* ''Handling:'' Lysozyme is a small, positively charged protein produced by monocytes; it is freely filtered by glomeruli and reabsorbed by proximal tubules.
* ''Proteinuria:'' Overproduction in these leukemias can cause nephrotic-range proteinuria from urinary lysozyme (lysozymuria).

Sources: [[Santoriello et al. 2017, Table 2 (first 3 points), p. 87|https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ekir.2016.09.002]].
